                <pb facs="0831" n="824" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg824"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.0146/601: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-12-20T20:00:00+00:00">December 20, 1937—8
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 20—3:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>790. Your 498, December 19, 3 p.m., was conveyed to Cadogan this afternoon. He
                    thanked me for the information and said that no moving of British troops in the
                    Shanghai area were contemplated at present. He said further that the Foreign
                    Office would be very glad to exchange views and advance information with respect
                    to any future reduction.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
